{"id":"forum-of-the-ox","name":"Forum of the Ox","qid":"Q4845769","country":"Turkey","locality":"Istanbul","lat":"41.01","lon":"28.95305556","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Date not recorded","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"","type":"square","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forum_of_the_Ox","text":"The Forum of the Ox (Latin: Forum Bovis, Greek: ὁ Bοῦς, meaning \"the Ox\") was a public square (Latin: Forum) in the city of Constantinople (today's Istanbul). Used also as a place for public executions and torture, it disappeared completely after the end of the Byzantine Empire.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forum_of_the_Ox","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-90b4340532a6","w":540,"h":1200,"title":"Bous Forumu.jpg","o":"gh-90b4340532a6.jpg","credit":{"text":"Özgür Arda BAYRAM","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bous_Forumu.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"assassins-creed-revelations--forum-of-the-ox","game":"assassins-creed-revelations","name":"Forum of the Ox","verified":false,"text":"the memory of the same name The Forum of the Ox, or Forum Bovis, was one of many forums built by the early Emperors of Nova Roma. Located in the Bayezid District of Constantinople, it was gradually built over by subsequent generations. In 1511, Ezio Auditore da Firenze learned that Niccolò Polo had hidden one of the Masyaf Keys beneath the Forum of the Ox.","text_source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Forum_of_the_Ox","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-777d1c11756c","w":1200,"h":660,"o":"gh-777d1c11756c.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Revelations, © the game's publisher.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:ACR_Forum_of_the_Ox_-_Concept_Art.jpg","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Crookandcharlata